// @run
// @log 0
// @hint Intentionally-unused parameter `_x` (leading `_` marks it unused)
// The GATE on D-ALIASARR, pinned from the side that would break if it were removed.
//
// `singleMemberAliasName` hands the emitter `tyToEmitName(m)`, and that renders a declared
// struct element STRUCTURALLY — `Cat[]` becomes `{n:i32}[]` — dropping the nominal name the
// emitter's element tables key on. That IS the "nominal emit route to lose" #1137 warned
// about, and it is load-bearing in exactly this shape: an array-of-declared-struct alias
// standing as a UNION ARM in a parameter compiles and runs, and becomes
// ``emitProgram: only i32, i64, f64, f32, boolean, struct, union, array, or string
// parameters are supported`` the moment the structural render is substituted for `L`.
//
// So the transparency arm is gated on `arrSpineIsScalar` — an array (of arrays…) whose LEAF
// element is a primitive, the condition under which the render is name-faithful. Five of the
// six alias bodies measured qualify; this one does not, and keeps the parent's behaviour in
// BOTH directions (this file runs on the parent too; `array-alias-transparent.vl` is what
// goes red there).
//
// Widening the arm to every `TyArray` turns this file red — which is the sabotage that says
// the gate is load-bearing rather than lazily narrow.
type Cat = { n: i32 }
type L = Cat[]

function tag(_x: L | i32) {
  return 0
}

print(tag(1))
